comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-12T02:57:25.496Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: all-status searches for GH-984, global --pm-path placement, plan show missing-id examples, and option-value-as-command found adjacent closed recovery item pm-185870 and open grammar conformance pm-fs8q9x, but no exact owner. Source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/984"
  "2026-08-12T02:57:42.017Z","harness:codex","Live reproduction during duplicate search: quoting the query '--pm-path before subcommand example path value' still caused the host-owned global option to be parsed out of the search argument and produced an Unknown option refusal for the search path. This confirms the same raw-argv/global-option ambiguity reaches ordinary agent recovery workflows; no item was claimed because this session is only documenting the newly reported owner."
